{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the two-blocker merge-plan repair at b9f3defdae017f1d6032c850c424395789fd8a0b (request/merge-plan-current, one commit on 88ac617c, parent verified; Rests-On repair request 93e0b0c5; exactly the six allowed files, +279/-616; six artifacts at the head cover exactly those paths; pushed; the original request/merge-plan branch untouched). Review against request 15321; not merged.\n\nBoth restated blockers are genuinely fixed, verified on a detached checkout. Blocker one: internal/mergeplan/mergeplan.go:735 now reads open, promised, reported, awaiting-merge, stale, and TestAllAndOnlyUnsettledCommitmentStatusesProtectCoveringArtifacts drives all ten statuses through Classify and PlanSuccession asserting both the class and the sealed LeftLive entry; removing awaiting-merge fails it at mergeplan_test.go:154 and :157, removing stale fails it, and adding satisfied fails it at :162 and :165, so the set is pinned in both directions. Against the live workroom with the same ratified approval and candidate, the four SKILL.md artifacts previously reported abandoned now classify as protected siblings under their commitments, and refs, .git/gitseq and main are byte-identical across the run. Blocker two: every named dead helper (coveredArtifacts, artifactCoversPath, protectionIndex, unsettledCommitment, provenanceClosure, withinReviewedPaths, artifactPath, canonicalCommit, canonicalPath, verdictSequence) and the test-only wrappers (successionPredecessors, planSuccession, successionCandidate) have zero references under cmd/; the eight Gitseq trailer constants, ReceiptKey, ReceiptRef and ReadReceipt have one definition each in internal/mergeplan with cmd/gs consuming them through an alias and one-line pass-throughs; go list -deps shows internal/mergeplan pulls no cmd/ package, so no cycle. No scope creep: docs, internal/app and cmd/gitseq-mcp are untouched, and the earlier advisories were correctly left alone. Gates: gofmt, go build, go vet,